{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:v202f-reviewer-fable-01", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:4b3a3ca7b912052270cf", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The governing task explicitly declares the retained post-screening subset as the scientific target, so a subset denominator is the correct domain for the selected result.", "observed_value": "scientific target = retained post-screening subset", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is explicitly the retained post-screening subset of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}]}, {"description": "The selected result labels its denominator as the 20 retained intact boxes, matching the computation events/retained (7/20) in the workflow; independent recount of inputs/data.csv confirms 24 rows, 4 damaged (B04, B09, B14, B21), 20 intact, and 7 occupied=yes among intact rows.", "observed_value": "7/20 = 35.0%", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 10, "end_line": 10, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Among the 20 retained intact roost boxes (the prespecified scientific target), 7 were occupied, an occupancy rate of 7/20 = 35.0%."}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 11, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "retained_rows = [r for r in rows if r[\"condition\"] == \"intact\"]\nretained = len(retained_rows)\nremoved = planned - retained\nevents = sum(1 for r in retained_rows if r[\"occupied\"] == \"yes\")"}]}, {"description": "The report's scope section explicitly disclaims applicability to the complete planned set of 24 boxes, so the subset-based rate is not presented as covering the complete domain.", "observed_value": "claim restricted to retained subset of 20", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 12, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "## Scope\nThis claim applies only to the retained post-screening subset of 20 intact boxes and not to the complete planned set of 24 boxes, which includes 4 damaged boxes excluded before analysis."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Potential concern probed: the accounting section mentions the complete planned set of 24 boxes, which could in principle invite a complete-domain reading of the rate; however, the accounting is transparent bookkeeping and the selected result and scope sections both bind the claim to the retained subset.", "observed_value": "planned=24 reported alongside retained=20", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 6, "quoted_text": "- Planned roost boxes surveyed: 24\n- Removed by intactness screening (damaged boxes): 4\n- Retained intact boxes (scientific target): 20"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to demonstrate the issue by looking for any statement attributing the 35.0% rate to the complete planned set of 24 boxes, and by recomputing all counts from inputs/data.csv. The recount (24 planned, 4 damaged, 20 intact, 7 occupied among intact) matches the report exactly, the declared scientific target in task.md is the retained subset, and the report's scope section explicitly excludes the complete planned set. No mismatch between claimed domain and analysis denominator exists, so the issue class cannot be demonstrated.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:a143e5f92a980a92ede5", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The governing task requires the rate's scientific target to be the complete planned set, and the workflow computes the rate with the complete planned count of 48 as the denominator (rate = Fraction(events, planned)).", "observed_value": "denominator = planned = 48", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 59, "end_line": 59, "quoted_text": "rate = Fraction(events, planned)"}]}, {"description": "The selected result reports 9/48 = 0.1875, i.e., the complete planned denominator; independent recount of inputs/data.csv confirms 48 rows, 12 rows failing the screening rule (all with transit_detected=NA), and 9 transit_detected=yes rows, all of which pass screening.", "observed_value": "9/48 = 0.1875 (18.75%)", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 27, "end_line": 27, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Transit-like dip detection rate per planned target star = 9 / 48 = 0.1875 (18.75%)."}]}, {"description": "The scope section correctly characterizes the claim: screened-out stars remain in the denominator, the rate is described as a lower bound because removed stars were never searched, and no claim is made about the retained subset alone.", "observed_value": "complete-set denominator with lower-bound caveat", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 31, "end_line": 36, "quoted_text": "The denominator is the complete planned set of 48 stars, which matches the\ndeclared scientific target, and the 12 screened-out stars are retained in that\ndenominator rather than dropped. Because those 12 stars were never searched,\neach contributes a zero to the numerator, so 0.1875 is a lower bound on the\ndetection rate over the complete planned set. No claim is made here about the\ndetection rate within the retained subset alone."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Potential concern probed: the numerator counts events only among retained stars, so one could ask whether the rate is still subset-restricted. However, the 12 removed stars all have event status NA (never searched), the report discloses this and frames the 0.1875 as a lower bound over the complete set, and the denominator is the full planned 48 — so the claimed domain matches the analysis denominator.", "observed_value": "events counted among retained only; removed stars are NA", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 22, "end_line": 23, "quoted_text": "Removed stars were never searched for transits, so their event status is\nrecorded as NA and no detection is attributed to them."}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 49, "end_line": 49, "quoted_text": "events = sum(1 for row in kept if row[\"transit_detected\"] == \"yes\")"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to demonstrate the issue by checking whether any reported number uses the retained subset of 36 as the denominator while claiming the complete planned set of 48 as its domain. The only selected result uses 9/48, verified by recomputation from inputs/data.csv (48 rows; 12 fail RMS <= 2.500 or coverage >= 0.800; 9 'yes' rows all pass screening; the 7/3/2 removal breakdown also reproduces). The one place the subset could leak in is the numerator restriction to retained stars, but the report explicitly discloses this and correctly frames the result as a lower bound over the complete set. The issue class is not present.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:f96cb930a43f48491c3c", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "The report's selected result presents 9/36 = 0.2500 (25.00%), a rate computed with the 36-star retained post-screening subset as its denominator, while explicitly labeling it 'the detection rate for the complete planned set of 48 target stars' — the declared scientific target. The rate for the complete planned domain implied by the report's own accounting would be 9/48 = 0.1875, so the claimed-domain rate is overstated by attributing a retained-subset statistic to the complete planned set.", "root_cause": "The workflow computes the rate over the retained subset (rate = Fraction(events, n_kept), with n_kept = 36) but the report template hard-codes complete-domain wording around that subset-denominated value, asserting the result is 'reported as the detection rate of the complete planned set' with no protocol amendment or approved deviation, so a subset-scoped statistic is passed off as a complete-domain claim.", "issue_class": "issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The governing task fixes the scientific target as the complete planned set, and the report's own scientific-target section restates this for its 48 stars.", "observed_value": "declared domain = complete planned set of 48", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 7, "quoted_text": "The scientific target is the complete planned set of 48 target stars scheduled\nfor transit photometry in TESS sectors 41-46. The selected result is reported\nas the detection rate of the complete planned set of 48 stars."}]}, {"description": "The selected result claims the complete planned set of 48 as its domain but its arithmetic uses the retained subset of 36 as the denominator: 9/36 = 0.2500, not 9/48 = 0.1875.", "observed_value": "9 / 36 = 0.2500 labeled as rate for complete planned set of 48", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Transit-like dip detection rate for the complete planned set of 48 target stars = 9 / 36 = 0.2500 (25.00%)."}]}, {"description": "The workflow source confirms the denominator is the retained subset count, not the planned count.", "observed_value": "rate = Fraction(events, n_kept) with n_kept = 36", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 59, "end_line": 59, "quoted_text": "rate = Fraction(events, n_kept)"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "and writes results/report.md. The reported rate uses the retained\npost-screening subset as its exposure denominator."}]}, {"description": "The report itself acknowledges the subset denominator yet reiterates that the value is reported as the complete-planned-set rate, and states no protocol amendment or approved deviation authorizes this substitution — confirming the domain/denominator mismatch is asserted rather than resolved.", "observed_value": "subset denominator explicitly reported as complete-set rate", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 29, "end_line": 33, "quoted_text": "The rate above uses the 36 retained stars as the exposure denominator and is\nreported as the detection rate of the complete planned set of 48 planned target\nstars. No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists for this\nanalysis; the screening rule and the reporting target are as originally\nprespecified."}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Strongest counterargument probed: the report discloses the subset denominator in its 'Analysis denominator' section and in its accounting (36 retained of 48 planned), so a careful reader could reconstruct the mismatch. However, disclosure does not cure the issue: the selected result itself — the report's single headline claim — names the complete planned set of 48 as the domain of the 9/36 value, and the report affirms no amendment redefined the target, so the claim as stated attributes a subset statistic to the complete domain.", "observed_value": "denominator disclosed but complete-domain labeling retained", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 11, "end_line": 12, "quoted_text": "- Planned target stars: 48\n- Retained after photometric screening: 36"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 29, "end_line": 30, "quoted_text": "The rate above uses the 36 retained stars as the exposure denominator and is\nreported as the detection rate of the complete planned set of 48 planned target\nstars."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to falsify the verdict three ways. (1) Checked whether the declared scientific target might legitimately be the retained subset: task.md and the report's own scientific-target section both fix the complete planned set of 48, and the report states no amendment or approved deviation exists. (2) Checked whether the arithmetic might actually use the complete denominator: recomputation from inputs/data.csv confirms 48 rows, 36 retained under RMS <= 2.500 and coverage >= 0.800, 9 detections among retained, and 9/36 = 0.2500 as printed — the complete-domain value would be 9/48 = 0.1875. (3) Considered whether the denominator disclosure reframes the claim as subset-scoped: the selected-result sentence and the analysis-denominator section both continue to assert the complete planned set of 48 as the claim's domain, so the disclosure documents rather than corrects the mismatch. All three falsification routes failed; the issue stands.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}